    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.21), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs near 5.00. **Gunnar Henderson** is our primary engine today, capitalizing on a weak matchup against Beck, while **Kyle Tucker** (80.37) rounds out the elite tier; the combination of a favorable wind blowing out and a soft matchup against Marte makes **Kyle Tucker** a high-leverage start for power and counting stats. We are also monitoring **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67), whose aggressive base-running profiles provide crucial support in our pursuit of the scarce stolen base category, especially with **Sam Antonacci** enjoying a strong platoon advantage and a leadoff spot against Sugano.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Jung** (45.92), who fell just outside the starting rotation. While **Josh Jung** carries a respectable projection, his score was suppressed by a matchup against the more capable Joe Ryan; the optimizer prioritized the higher-upside platoon edges provided by **Brayan Rocchio** and the lineup order advantages held by our core infielders. We continue to manage our roster depth carefully while navigating the absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL. Managers should be particularly wary of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Kyle Tucker**; while their scores are currently bolstered by assumed lineup slots, any significant drop in their batting order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores before first pitch.",
